/*
===========================================================================

dhewm3-rt Vulkan — fsr_tc_mask.comp — FSR 2 transparency-and-composition mask.

Extracts the per-pixel T&C class the G-buffer prepass stashed in gbufAlbedo's
alpha channel into a standalone R8 mask, which is the shape
ffxFsr2ContextDispatch wants for transparencyAndComposition.

Alpha carries the mask because gbufAlbedo's rgb is the only part anything reads
(gi_albedo_mod.comp) and its alpha was a constant 1.0 — a free render-resolution
channel that avoids a fifth colour attachment and the ten pipeline-creation
sites that would come with one.

The prepass writes 1.0 - tcClass, so:
  alpha == 1.0  ->  mask 0  (ordinary surface, or a pixel the prepass never
                             wrote: sky and translucents clear to white)
  alpha <  1.0  ->  mask 1 - alpha

FSR 2's depth-clip pass already 3x3 max-dilates whatever it is given
(PreProcessReactiveMasks, ffx_fsr2_depth_clip.h), so no dilation happens here.

Descriptors (set 0):
  binding 0 — srcAlbedo sampler2D    (gbufAlbedo; texelFetch only)
  binding 1 — dstMask   r8 storage image (tcMask)

Push constants (8 bytes, matches FsrTcMaskPC in vk_upscale.cpp):
  ivec2 renderExtent — valid sub-rect of both images

FSR upscaling arc U4 — docs/plans/20260918_fsr_upscaling.md §9.

This file is a new addition with dhewm3-rt.  It was created with the aid of GenAI,
and may reference the existing Dhewm3 OpenGL and vkDoom3 Vulkan updates of the Doom 3 GPL Source
Code.

It is distributed under the same modified GNU General Public License Version 3 of the original Doom 3 GPL Source
Code release.

===========================================================================
*/

#version 460
layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8) in;

layout(set = 0, binding = 0) uniform sampler2D srcAlbedo;
layout(set = 0, binding = 1, r8) uniform image2D dstMask;

layout(push_constant) uniform PC {
    ivec2 renderExtent;
} pc;

void main()
{
    ivec2 coord = ivec2(gl_GlobalInvocationID.xy);
    if (coord.x >= pc.renderExtent.x || coord.y >= pc.renderExtent.y)
        return;

    float packed = texelFetch(srcAlbedo, coord, 0).a;
    imageStore(dstMask, coord, vec4(clamp(1.0 - packed, 0.0, 1.0)));
}
